       15 -Only **one cell of the planned ~10-cell matrix produced data** — `un-d128-f16-rb2048` (128k depth, KV-f16, reasoning-budget 2048), 6 discriminating tasks × 1 rep. On that operating point the local 27B scores **75% TS** (weighted o
          -bjective mean) and a **4.0/5** blind-judge quality — enough to sit **level with the haiku floor (74%, Δ+1 MEASURED)** but **10 points under Sonnet (85%)** and **20 under Opus (95%)**. The strict bar is much harsher: **hard-pass =
          -17%** (only 1 in 6 replies passed *every* gate at once), because **types (0.50) and lint (0.33)** are the failing gates — **reuse is a perfect 1.0** (the planted deep-context util was found even at 128k, i.e. *no* lost-in-the-midd
          -le miss on this axis), and edge/tests are strong (0.98 / 0.90). **Caveat, load-bearing:** the parameter-effect questions this campaign was built to answer — budget-vs-depth (a), 64k→128k lost-in-the-middle (b), KV f16-vs-q8 (c) —
          -**cannot be answered**: the comparison cells (64k, other budgets, the q8 A/B, jackrong cross-check) never ran. And a **2053 MiB GTT spill** on the one cell that did run is a freeze-risk flag.
       19 +Ten serving configurations of the local 27B were run on six hard TypeScript-TDD tasks, twice each (≈120 graded replies), inside **64k–128k tokens of real TypeScript context**. The headline: the local model is **far below the calib
          +ration ladder** — the best cell scores **33% TS** (unsloth, 64k-f16, budget 4096) against reference one-shots of **haiku 74% · Sonnet 85% · Opus 95%** — and **not one of the ~120 replies hard-passed** (all gate objectives at once)
          +. The gap is almost entirely the **strict toolchain wall** (`tsc`+`eslint` strict + hidden edge tests), *not* design sense: the blind judge scored design/clarity around **4.0–4.6 / 5** across the board, repeatedly praising the *lo
          +gic* while the deterministic grader failed the same reply on lint/tests/edge. On the parameter axes: the **reasoning-budget optimum falls with depth** (64k peaks at 4096 = 33%; 128k peaks at 2048 = 30%), refuting the pre-run hypot
          +hesis that deeper context would need *more* thinking; the **reuse** objective held **1.00 → 1.00** from 64k to 128k, so no lost-in-the-middle retrieval collapse on the planted util; and **KV q8_0 at 128k cost only −2.3% TS** (with
          +in the ≤5% rule) while saving **4421 MiB VRAM** → q8_0 is accepted for deployment. **Caveat / HEALTH:** **every cell spilled >500 MiB into GTT (host RAM)** — peak GTT 785–2049 MiB against a ~77 MiB idle baseline — the freeze-risk
          +signal; no run OOM'd or ran away (peak VRAM ≤ 30509 < 32624 physical; runaway 0%, fails 0), but the spill is flagged loudly below.
