       50 -## Campaign questions — answered vs unmeasured
       69 +### (a) Budget optimum vs depth — does it rise with depth? **No — it falls.** (MEASURED)
       70 +unsloth-f16 TS% by budget: **64k** — 1024→26%, 2048→28%, **4096→33% (peak)**; **128k** — 1024→24%,
       71 +**2048→30% (peak)**, 4096→26%. The optimum **moves down** from budget 4096 at 64k to 2048 at 128k.
       72 +This **refutes** the pre-run hypothesis (README §6, `INFERRED` from C2) that deeper context would push
       73 +the reasoning optimum *up*. **INFERRED explanation:** at 128k the extra thinking at 4096 does not buy
       74 +accuracy back (26% < the 30% at 2048) — plausibly the longer reasoning trajectory drifts or the model
       75 +is context-bound rather than think-bound at depth; either way, spending more thinking tokens at 128k is
       76 +a net loss. **Consequence for practice:** budget **2048** is the safe deploy point at 128k; budget
       77 +4096 only pays off at the shallower 64k depth.
       78
