      125 -## Methodology & caveats
      126 -
      127 -- **Eval:** 6 discriminating TypeScript-TDD tasks (Sonnet-tier `lru-cache`/`rate-limiter`/`store-remove`/`deep-equal` + Opus-tier `async-memo`/`expr-eval`), graded by the **real toolchain** (`tsc` + `eslint` strict + `vitest`, plu
          -s a hidden edge suite and a planted-util reuse check). Blind LLM judge (opus subagent) adds design/clarity/robustness. Full detail: `eval-design.md`.
      128 -- **n = 6 replies, ×1 rep** on the single cell (below the engine-bench REPS ≥ 2 standard — another reason to treat the point as indicative, not settled).
      129 -- **Reference bands** (haiku 74.2 / Sonnet 85.1 / Opus 95.4) are the campaign's calibration scores (MEASURED, `summary.json`), drawn as lines on the quality charts.
      130 -- **Provenance:** every number here is MEASURED from `out/summary.md`, `out/summary.json`, `charts/appendix.md`; reasoning is tagged INFERRED; no external CLAIMED numbers used. The three unanswered questions are marked UNMEASURED/
          -OPEN — nothing invented to fill them.
      131 -- **Biggest gap:** this is a **partial run**. To close the campaign, re-run the missing cells (`bash run_capture.sh` is resumable — finished cells skip) with priority on the **128k q8_0 A/B** (memory + question c) and the **64k de
          -pth twin** (question b), then the budget sweep (question a).
